@Contents
$ #SEFP2 version 1.2.0.145#
System requirements: Win2K+ / FAR 2.0.1420+

  ~What is SEFP2~@hcWhatIs@

  ~Configure plugin~@hcConfigure@

  ~Supported Phones~@hcSupportedPhones@

  ~Connecting a phone~@hcConnect@

  ~Working with a phone~@hcWork@


Visit us: #www.davinciteam.com#

@hcWhatIs
$ #SEFP2 - What is PhoneFS#
  #SEFP2# brings all the power of #Far  Manager#  to  SEMC mobile phone's
internal filesystem. SEFP2 uses native SEMC protocol to access files. You can work with folders
as easy as with single file. SEFP2 recursively process all files insidea folder. 
On a progress screen during the process You can see:


   -#Source and Destanation filenames#

   -#Current file progress bar#

   -#Total files size information#

   -#Total progress bar#

   -#Number of files processed/total#

   -#Time elapsed and estimate#

   -#Current transfer speed#




  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@hcConfigure
$ #SEFP2 - Configure plugin#
  Before the beginning of work with SEFP2, You need to adjust  some
parameters. To enter in the configuration menu, choose #SEFP2# from
the Far menu #Options#/#Plugins configuration#:


   #Add to Plugins menu#         - leave checked if You want to  see 
PhoneFS in Plugins dialog #F11#

   #Add to Disks menu#           - leave checked to be able to select
PhoneFS from Disks menu #Alt+F1/Alt+F2#

   #Disks menu hotkey ('1'-'9')# - set desired hotkey for Disks menu.
Leave blank for autoassign



 
  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

