@hcSupportedActions
$ #SEFP2 - Actions available table#

 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 Domain |        RED            |       BROWN            | SUPERCID
 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 CID    |36 49 50 51 52 53 80 81| 36 49 50 51 52 53 80 81|   ANY
 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 DB2010 |WO WO -- -- -- -- -- --| RW RW -- -- -- -- -- --|   RW
 DB2012 |-- -- WO WO WO WO -- --| -- -- RW RW -- -- -- --|   RW
 DB2020 |-- WO -- WO WO WO -- --| RW RW -- -- -- -- -- --|   RW
 PNX5230|-- -- -- WO WO WO -- --| -- RW -- RW RW -- -- --|   --
 DB3150 |-- RW -- RW RW -- -- --| -- RW -- RW RW -- -- --|   RW
 DB3200 |-- RW -- RW RW WO WO WO| -- RW -- RW RW RW RW RW|   RW
 DB3210 |-- RW -- RW RW WO WO WO| -- RW -- RW RW RW RW RW|   RW
 DB3350 |-- RW -- RW RW WO WO WO| -- RW -- RW RW RW RW RW|   RW
-------------------------------------------------------------------

 RW - Reading, writing and access attributes available
 WO - Writing only available
 -- - Not exists / not supported
 Files and folders delete supported in any CID/Color combination

 RED      - Retail product (PRODUCT)
 BROWN    - Developer device (R&D)
 BLUE     - Factory device (FACTORY)
 SUPERCID - Security disabled device. Any color



  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@hcWork
$ #SEFP2 - Working with a phone#
  SEFP2 allows You to work with a phone filesystem absolutely the same way
as You doing it with a local drive:


  #F5#/#F6#          - Copy/move a file/folder from/to the local disk.

  #F7#             - Create a new folder on a phone.

  #F8#             - Delete file/folder from a phone.

  #Alt+F7#         - Find files




  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@

@hcConnect
$ #SEFP2 - Connecting a phone#
   You can open SEFP2 from Disks Menu #Alt+F1#/#Alt+F2# or from Plugins
Dialog #F11#. No additional software (PC Suite etc.) required for SEFP2 
to work. You need to have USB flashing cable drivers only.


  ~SonyEricsson~

   Before connect the phone You need to make sure battery is fully charged, 
otherwise You can lose some data.
Phone can be connected by USB cable. #DCU-60# / #DCU-65# is the cable that comes 
with phone in a box. Drivers You can find in Download Area at #www.davinciteam.com# 
To connect a phone You need:
-Power OFF the phone and reinsert battery
-Open SEFP2 start dialog and press Connect
-Connect USB cable holding #C# button






  ~Go to main screen~@Contents@
